From 240e341917963fe604f0b42bd3693baa53c67538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:33:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(Detective #121): the structured family's field and
 class operators are pinned by intent tests

The defect, verbatim. "`field` is not generated. The catalog marks it `unsupported`. Its reason: the
observed codomain is a bare type name. It cannot show that a return is a record, nor its fields' types."
"`class` is not generated ... a super- or sub-type instance has to be constructed, and no total
construction follows from a type name." "A record return gets only the universal operators. Probed:
`midpoint(a, b) -> Point` (observed `{Point}`) gets `return_none`, `return_const`, `return_identity` and
`return_stale`. A namedtuple observed under its class name gets no tuple operator either."

Why the obvious fix is wrong. A runtime dispatch on "is this a record?" is a no-op wherever the premise
fails (a built-in survivor), and rebuilding the record by calling its constructor re-runs its validation,
which can raise. The baseline run observes the instances themselves (38bec04), so the field names and types
are READ OFF them, and the perturbation works on a COPY with the field written past `__setattr__` and
`__post_init__` (a record that is inconsistent on purpose), never the original.

What each state means. Per return site: `return_field_drop@<f>` (a field to its type's default, builtin
kinds only: never a constructor that could run user code), `return_field_bump@<f>` (a numeric, boolean, str
or bytes field moved a step), `return_field_swap@<a>,<b>` (a field exchanged with the previous field of its
type): one mutant per field, the field in the mode, from a dataclass, namedtuple, attrs class or plain
object (`__dict__` or `__slots__`). `return_class_subclass` returns a copy rebound to a dynamically created
subclass that reads the same (name, module, qualname) and shares its layout: it passes `isinstance` and
fails `type(x) is C`. `return_class_base` returns a copy rebound to the first user base class. A site that
returned records of two shapes offers no field mutant, a class whose copy is itself (an enum member) offers
neither class mutant and the function's `mu_minus_withheld` names it.

What was NOT closed. Detective's harvest still carries type names (see 38bec04), so a Detective
`--two-sign` run does not yet generate these. attrs is covered through `__attrs_attrs__` without importing
attrs and no test imports it. A class with `__init_subclass__` side effects runs them once per process when
its subclass is built. A dynamic-subclass instance reprs like the class it copies, so a test that compares
reprs does not see it (that is the point of the operator).

Sensitivity: with the class and field candidates removed 11 of the 25 intent tests fail.
Pin: the pure decisions are pinned in 38bec04.

Tests: tests/test_mu_minus_structured_premise_intent.py 25 passed; with the catalog, doc, policy and
instrumentation-ownership guards 96 passed under Python 3.14 and 96 under 3.12, PYTHONUNBUFFERED unset.
ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
